%N A399339 The binomial matrix of the Polya tree numbers, square array read by ascending antidiagonals.
%C A399339 See the comments and links in A399000.
%H A399339 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://github.com/PeterLuschny/Gists/blob/main/GnomonicExpansionAndBinomialMatrices.ipynb">Gnomonic Expansion and Binomial Matrices</a>, a Python notebook.
%F A399339 A(n, n) = P(n) := A000081(n) if n > 0, P(0) = 1.
%F A399339 A(n, k) = Sum_{m=0..d} binomial(d, m) * s^(d - m) * P(p + m), where d = abs(n - k), p = min(n, k), s = 1 if k <= n, otherwise -1.
%e A399339 Array begins:
%e A399339   [0]    1,    0,   0,   1,  -1,   3,  -4,  12, -24, ...
